<div><span class="mfg-kicker">WHERE THE INTERFACES MATTER</span><h2>A board, a housing and a fixture should share the same requirements.</h2><p>Connector positions, mounting datums, assembly access and test points affect more than one supplier. Reviewing them together helps expose fit and testability issues before a build is released.</p><a href="/contact.html?service=manufacturing#project-inquiry" class="mfg-text-link">Talk through your assembly ↗</a></div>
<div class="mfg-interface-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Board to enclosure</h3><p>Align outlines, connector cut-outs, mounting holes, thermal paths and access for assembly.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Part to fixture</h3><p>Define locating datums, clamping surfaces, operator access and the features to inspect.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Build to acceptance</h3><p>Agree drawing revisions, sample approval, inspection records and functional test coverage.</p></div></article></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="mfg-heading"><div><span class="mfg-kicker">FROM RFQ TO HANDOVER</span><h2>A clear route into production.</h2></div><p>Scope, manufacturing capabilities and acceptance criteria are reviewed for each project. Materials, tolerances, quantities and lead times are confirmed in the quotation.</p></div>
<div class="mfg-process"><article><span>01 / REVIEW</span><h3>Send the brief</h3><p>Share the application, drawing revisions, quantities, target date and destination.</p></article><article><span>02 / DEFINE</span><h3>Close the open points</h3><p>Review manufacturability, critical features, sourcing and inspection requirements.</p></article><article><span>03 / BUILD</span><h3>Approve and execute</h3><p>Agree the quotation and sample plan, then coordinate the build and approved changes.</p></article><article><span>04 / DELIVER</span><h3>Review the evidence</h3><p>Complete agreed acceptance checks, documentation, packaging and shipping arrangements.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section mfg-rfq" id="rfq"><div class="container mfg-rfq-grid"><div><span class="mfg-kicker">START YOUR RFQ</span><h2>Have a drawing?<br>Let’s define the build.</h2><p>Tell us what you need made and where it needs to go. We will review the inputs and clarify the scope before quoting.</p><a href="/contact.html?service=manufacturing#project-inquiry" class="btn btn-light">Request A Manufacturing Quote ↗</a><p class="mfg-rfq-note">Contact us to agree confidentiality arrangements and a suitable file-sharing channel.</p></div><div class="mfg-rfq-checklist"><h3>What to prepare</h3><ul><li><strong>Mechanical parts</strong><span>STEP model, dimensioned PDF, material, finish and critical tolerances.</span></li><li><strong>Jigs & fixtures</strong><span>Part data, operation, locating requirements and acceptance method.</span></li><li><strong>PCBA</strong><span>BOM, Gerber or fabrication data, placement files and test requirements.</span></li><li><strong>Every inquiry</strong><span>Quantity, revision, target schedule and delivery country.</span></li></ul></div></div></section>
